{"name":"Buckeye","hex":"#674834","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Buckeye","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A native or resident of the American states of Ohio or Arizona."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A number of places in the United States:\nA city in Maricopa County, Arizona.\nAn unincorporated community in El Dorado County, California.\nA former travel station in Plumas County, California.\nAn unincorporated community in Yolo County, California, named for buckeye trees there.\nFormer name of Carbondale, Amador County, California.\nAn unincorporated community in Larimer County, Colorado.\nAn unincorporated community in Salamonie Township, Huntingdon County, Indiana.\nA minor city in Hardin County, Iowa.\nAn unincorporated community in Dickinson County, Kansas.\nAn unincorporated community in Garrard County, Kentucky.\nAn unincorporated community in Mississippi County, Missouri, named for buckeye trees.\nAn unincorporated community in Milton Township, Jackson County, Ohio, named after the Buckeye Furnace.\nAn unincorporated community in Spokane County, Washington, named after the Buckeye Lumber Co.\nAn unincorporated community in Pocahontas County, West Virginia, named after Buckeye Cove.\nA number of townships in the United States, listed under Buckeye Township.","A city in Maricopa County, Arizona."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Buckeye"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ohio","blocks":[{"text":"Ohio is a state in the Midwestern region of the United States. It borders the Canadian province of Ontario to the north, Pennsylvania to the east, West Virginia to the southeast, Kentucky to the southwest, Indiana to the west, and Michigan to the northwest. Ohio is the 34th-largest state by area, at 44,825 sq mi (116,100 km2), and the seventh-most populous state, with a population of nearly 11.9 million. Its capital and most populous city is Columbus, with other major metropolitan cities including Cleveland, Cincinnati, Dayton, Akron, and Toledo."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Flag_of_Ohio.svg/330px-Flag_of_Ohio.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ohio"},{"title":"Ohio State Buckeyes","blocks":[{"text":"The Ohio State Buckeyes are the intercollegiate athletic teams that represent Ohio State University, located in Columbus, Ohio. The athletic programs are named after the colloquial term for people from the state of Ohio and after the state tree, the Ohio buckeye. The Buckeyes participate in the National Collegiate Athletic Association's (NCAA) Division I and the Big Ten Conference in most sports. The Ohio State women's ice hockey team competes in the Western Collegiate Hockey Association (WCHA). The school colors are scarlet and gray. The university's mascot is Brutus Buckeye. \"THE\" is the official trademark of the Ohio State University merchandise. Led by its football program, the Buckeyes have the largest overall sports endowment of any campus in North America."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Ohio_State_Buckeyes_logo.svg/330px-Ohio_State_Buckeyes_logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ohio_State_Buckeyes"},{"title":"Buckeye (candy)","blocks":[{"text":"Buckeyes are confections made from a peanut butter fudge partially dipped in chocolate to leave a circle of peanut butter visible. Buckeyes are similar to peanut butter balls, which are completely covered in chocolate. While similar to the more widely known Reese's cup, the buckeye has a higher ratio of peanut butter to chocolate and a smoother texture due to the use of powdered sugar to make the peanut butter into a fudge. Buckeye candies are also often stored in the fridge or freezer giving a snap to the chocolate coating."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Buckeyes_Peanut_Butter_Balls%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Buckeyes_Peanut_Butter_Balls%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buckeye_(candy)"},{"title":"Buckeye (novel)","blocks":[{"text":"Buckeye is a historical fiction novel by Patrick Ryan. The book follows two couples from the fictional town of Bonhomie, Ohio from World War II to the end of the 20th century and the secrets which develop between them. It is Ryan's first full length novel for adults and received favorable reviews from critics."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f4/Buckeye_book_cover.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buckeye_(novel)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/2002_OH_Proof.png/500px-2002_OH_Proof.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/2002_OH_Proof.png/500px-2002_OH_Proof.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A2002_OH_Proof.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Sunwatch_Aerial_illustration_HRoe_2018_400px.jpg/330px-Sunwatch_Aerial_illustration_HRoe_2018_400px.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Sunwatch_Aerial_illustration_HRoe_2018_400px.jpg/330px-Sunwatch_Aerial_illustration_HRoe_2018_400px.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Artist's conception of the Fort Ancient culture SunWatch Indian Village in present-day Dayton, Ohio","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASunwatch_Aerial_illustration_HRoe_2018_400px.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/5Nati